# Lobe Chat Project Intelligence

This file captures important patterns, preferences, and project-specific intelligence to help work effectively with the Lobe Chat codebase.

## Project Structure Patterns

- The project follows a Next.js App Router structure with `/src/app` as the main application directory
- Monorepo structure with packages in the `/packages` directory
- Extensive internationalization with language files in `/locales` directory 
- Documentation maintained in `/docs` with multilingual support
- Configuration files at the root level with a preference for JavaScript format (.js extensions)
- Docker configuration for various deployment options

## Code Style Preferences

- TypeScript is used throughout the codebase
- Configuration files use JavaScript with CommonJS or ESM syntax
- ESLint, Prettier, and Stylelint are used for code quality
- Conventional commits are used for version control (based on commitlint config)
- Unit tests are written with Vitest

## Development Workflow

- pnpm is used as the package manager (not npm or yarn)
- The project appears to follow a feature-branch workflow
- Changesets or similar are likely used for release management
- Docker is used for containerized development and deployment
- Comprehensive documentation is maintained for contributors

## Observed Architectural Patterns

- Zustand is used for state management
- The app likely follows a component-based architecture
- Internationalization appears to be a first-class concern
- API routes are likely implemented within the Next.js framework
- Multiple authentication providers are supported

## Project Preferences

- Detailed documentation is valued (extensive docs directory)
- Multilingual support is prioritized (multiple locale files)
- Self-hosting capabilities are important (Docker configurations)
- Testing is emphasized (Vitest configuration)

